course: dictionary
lesson: 6376
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word mug can be a cup, a drink, or an action word about robbery. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. «She poured a mug of cocoa» means the cup and what is in it.
explain: «A shiny glaze, which is a thin coat of glass, makes a mug waterproof.» Here a mug is the cup you hold. Ask yourself: does this still make sense if I put cup in its place? If yes, you have the right meaning.
explain: Mug can also be a verb, a word for an action. «Being mugged means being robbed in the street.» This meaning is serious, so the lesson is about staying safe, not about being brave: let things go, get away, and tell a grown-up.
explain: Informal talk adds more meanings. In British slang, a mug can be a face, or a silly person who is easily tricked. The clues around the word show which one you need. When you are not sure, check a dictionary.
fact: A mug is a big cup with straight sides and a handle, used for hot drinks.
fact: «A mug of cocoa» means the drink inside the cup.
fact: To mug someone means to attack and rob them, usually in the street.
fact: Hot drinks can scald, so carry a mug carefully and keep it away from small children and the edges of tables.
fact: Informally, mug can mean a face, and in British slang a silly person who is easily tricked.
exercise: «She held a warm mug of tea in both hands.» What is a mug here? | *A big cup with a handle, for hot drinks | A silly person who is easily tricked | To attack someone in the street | A face
exercise: «Two men tried to mug the old man near the bus stop.» What does mug mean in this sentence? | To hug | To wash up | To smile | *To attack and rob
exercise: «Small cups for juice hold 200 or 250 ml, a mug about 300 ml.» Which holds more? | *A mug, about 300 ml | They hold the same amount | Neither holds anything | A small juice cup, 200 or 250 ml
test: «She poured a mug of cocoa for her little brother.» In this sentence, what does mug mean? | A silly person | A cup | *The drink in the cup | A robbery
test: If someone tries to mug you, what should you do? | Stay and argue about your phone | *Let things go, get away, and tell an adult | Fight them back | Shout and chase them after they run
exam: In «He pulled a funny mug at the teacher», what does mug mean? | *A face | A cup | A drink | To attack and rob
